{"content":"Now I have a comprehensive picture. Let me compile the distinct enforcement sites:\n\nh15.\n\nMemo visibility is enforced at these distinct server-side sites:\n\n1. **GetMemo / single-memo read gate** (`checkMemoReadAccess`) — `server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go` (line 39–67, called at lines 356, 367)\n2. **ListMemos query-level visibility filter** — `server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go` (lines 218–227, injects `VisibilityList` / filter into the store query)\n3. **ListMemoComments query-level visibility filter** — `server/router/api/v1/memo_service_comments.go` (lines 148–161, calls `checkMemoReadAccess` on the parent and applies a visibility filter to comment listing)\n4. **CreateMemoComment — parent memo visibility check** — `server/router/api/v1/memo_service_comments.go` (lines 33–43, blocks commenting on a `PRIVATE` memo by non-owners)\n5. **ListMemoRelations visibility filter** — `server/router/api/v1/memo_relation_service.go` (lines 107–112, passes a `memoFilter` scoped by visibility to the store)\n6. **Batch relation conversion visibility filter** — `server/router/api/v1/memo_service_converter.go` (lines 182–187, applies the same visibility filter when batch-loading relations for listed memos)\n7. **Attachment access gate** (`checkAttachmentAccess`) — `server/router/api/v1/attachment_service.go` (lines 420–455, enforces the linked memo's visibility on `GetAttachment`)\n8. **ListMemoAttachments visibility check** — `server/router/api/v1/memo_attachment_service.go` (lines 213–225, checks memo visibility before listing its attachments)\n9. **User stats visibility filter** — `server/router/api/v1/user_service_stats.go` (lines 83–91, restricts which memos count toward stats based on viewer identity)\n10. **SSE delivery filtering** (`canReceive`) — `server/router/api/v1/sse_hub.go` (lines 134–144, `PRIVATE` events are only delivered to the owner or admins)\n11. **Inbox / notification visibility guard** (`canViewerAccessMemo`) — `server/router/api/v1/user_service_notifications.go` (lines 302–316, gates whether a notification is generated/sent based on memo visibility)\n12. **Email notification visibility guard** (`canViewerAccessMemo`) — `server/notification/email.go` (lines 306–320, same pattern — suppresses email notifications for private/protected memos the recipient can't access)\n13. **Mention notification suppression** (`canUserAccessMentionContext`) — `server/router/api/v1/memo_mention_helpers.go` (lines 56–72, skips mention inbox items when the mentioned user cannot see the memo due to `PRIVATE` visibility)","iteration":10,"turn":1,"type":"assistant"}
